# Owner preferences (Idle Party)

Source: owner answers (vibe-coder). Agents follow these without re-asking.
Last preference sync: **2026-08-13** (workstyle: commit locally when a batch is
verified; still ask before push / Play / save-wipe. Product locks unchanged).

## Near-term focus

- **Default roadmap:** follow `docs/STRATEGY_90D.md` — Month 1 chase/first-hour → Month 2 kits fairness+fantasy → Month 3 zone identity (blueprint). Don’t invent a competing priority list. **Now:** Month 1 (chase / first hour).
- Vague “gör spelet bättre / vad härnäst” → **do the current month**, not `/init`, cleanup, or CI chores.
- Prefer **game feel / content** over Play ops busywork (closed-test recruitment can idle in background).
- Play production remains a goal, but day-to-day work defaults to **content + feel** unless the owner asks about Play.
- Background why (optional read): `docs/TOP_GAMES_RESEARCH.md`.

## Distribution

- Goal: **Google Play “for real” soon** (not sideload-only forever).
- Prefer work that unblocks Play when touching store: CI signing secrets, closed-test 12×14, production access — see `docs/PLAY_STORE.md`.
- **Current fact:** GitHub Releases (APK/AAB) is still the primary install path. Play Console app `com.idleparty.app` exists (listing + closed Alpha); **production is not live**.
- **Platforms now:** Android (+ existing web playtest tooling OK). **No iOS** and **no shipping web as a product** for now.

## UI target device (mandatory)

- **Phone-only product.** Design and ship for portrait phones (~360–430 CSS px wide). Do not optimize for desktop/tablet layouts as the real product.
- **Owner reference phone: Samsung Galaxy A56** (1080×2340 @ DPR 3 → **360×780** CSS). Cursor browser playtest must always emulate this (or equivalent 360-wide portrait) via CDP device metrics — never judge UI at desktop/tablet width.
- Hub, GEAR/BAG, menus, tooltips, touch targets: assume **finger + portrait**. Hover-only UX is playtest-only; phone must work with tap / long-press.
- Flutter **web** remains a Cursor playtest harness with **forced phone emulation** — never treat wide desktop chrome as the shipping UI.
- **Owner play notes win.** If they write what the first hour felt like (TODAY lied, tips got in the way, “what do I chase?”), that *is* the Month 1 batch — fix those surfaces. Don’t wait for a formal audit. Don’t invent a 10-minute phone pass without their notes unless they asked you to playtest in the Cursor browser.

## Work style

- Prefer **large batches** (“gör allt X”) — fewer tiny back-and-forths.
- Still verify (analyze/tests / hub smoke as needed) before calling done.
- **Commit locally** when the requested batch is verified (DoD). Don’t wait for
  a second “ska jag commita?”. **Ask before push, PR, and release tags.** Never
  force-push or skip hooks unless the owner says so in that turn.
- **Code shape:** prefer splitting a giant file (`game_logic`, `is2_shell`,
  `spatial_combat`, …) when a change needs a home. Do **not** merge more into
  those files. Keep SpatialCombat as combat authority (extract helpers, don’t
  add a second fight sim).
- **Dead code:** delete unused files/APIs with zero callers. Keep JSON/save
  fields that old saves may still contain (`save-migrate`). Unused
  `@Deprecated` helpers that are not serialized may go.
- **Git:** daily work on `main`. `release/x.y.z` only when cutting a tag. Don’t open a release branch for chores.
- **Don’t stage** `windows/flutter/generated_*` unless `pubspec.yaml` plugins actually changed (`jni` noise from `pub get` is not a product change).
- **Product locks stay** (phone, English UI, fairness, no IAP, 90-day roadmap,
  legal/Kenney). Agents may tighten *workstyle* so they can finish; they must
  not weaken those locks. Cursor/AI safety (no exploits, no foreign dumps) is
  not overridable from this file.

## Game feel & fantasy

- First-hour / player fantasy priority: **progression / power** (grow the party, feel stronger).
- Keep hub/UI **readable and low-panic** (not sweaty esports chrome).
- **Early game:** approachable. **Endgame** (high AL / Gauntlet / late zones): OK to be **competitive / grindy**.
- Challenges/Gauntlet are welcome depth; don’t make the first hour feel like a raid.

## Content priorities

- **Kits:** polish what exists (fairness + clarity + fantasy) before adding many new specs.
- **Zones:** prefer **more zones** when adding content (still use `zone-art-identity` so they don’t feel like reskins).
- **Meta loops** (daily vault / Will / Gauntlet / season): push toward **“I always know what I’m chasing today”** — hub TODAY with READY/ALMOST, Ascend Blessing + unlock teasers, clear claims.
- **God Hand:** owner undecided (fun steer vs deeper strategy) — don’t redesign GH direction without asking.
- **Monetization:** **no IAP / no paid store** for a while longer (stay free, no ads unless owner revisits).

## Language

- **In-game copy stays English** (UI, tips, What’s New, guides).
- Agent ↔ owner chat: plain Swedish (or their language). No jargon quizzes.

## Balance vs fantasy

**Owner choice: fairness first (rättvisa först).**

When a kit is fun but share/CI says HIGH (or clearly stomps peers):

1. Trim until live-light gate / ±20% share band is honest — fantasy second.
2. Keep *identity* if possible (names, VFX, rotation shape) but numbers must come in line.
3. Plain Swedish one-liner when done: “för stark → sänkt så den matchar andra.”
4. Do **not** leave documented HIGH outliers “for flavor” without an explicit later override.

